{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The internal hard drive fits my past desktop upgrades, and the HDMI cable relates to my display-cable purchase, although neither gives me a reason to buy immediately.",
    "Wired earbuds with a microphone connect to my previous headset purchase because they serve a similar listening and calling purpose."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Buying a small-tablet mount does not mean I need another tablet or a wall mount for a television; those purchases solve different problems.",
    "The memory cards and USB-B cable require a specific compatible device and an actual need that my history does not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases of computer accessories seem to have been treated as interest in almost any electronics accessory.",
    "Owning an accessory for a device seems to have been taken as a reason to recommend another device or loosely related accessories."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My purchases are years apart, and I rarely buy unless something solves a particular problem; a related item alone is not enough.",
    "The connector, compatibility, and purpose matter to me: my recent Ethernet adapter addressed connectivity, which does not imply a need for memory cards or a printer cable."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in practical electronics upgrades but assume more current needs than my occasional, specific purchases support."
}"}
